-- title:
--   ℚ-fibre of the ℤ_{(ℓ)}-chart algebra of the Igusa model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$, a prime $\ell$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Let $S$ be an arbitrary subset of $F$. Consider two subalgebras of $F$: `chartAlg N ℓ S`, the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[S] =$ `Algebra.adjoin ℤℓ S`, and [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.chartRing ℚ S`](def/JacJ1_ChartAlgebra.html#L45), the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Q}[S] =$ `Algebra.adjoin ℚ S`. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebras
--   $$e \colon \mathbb{Q} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathrm{chartAlg}(N,\ell,S) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{chartRing}_{\mathbb{Q}}(S)$$
--   which is compatible with multiplication inside $F$: for every $q \in \mathbb{Q}$ and every $b$ in `chartAlg N ℓ S`, the image of $e(q \otimes b)$ in $F$ equals $q \cdot b$, the scalar multiple of (the image of) $b$ by $q$. Thus the isomorphism is not merely abstract but is the one induced by the multiplication map into $F$.
--
--   This is the statement that localisation commutes with the formation of integral closures, in the form needed here: inverting all nonzero integers turns the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[S]$ in the modular function field into the integral closure of $\mathbb{Q}[S]$ there. It is used to identify the generic fibres of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-charts of the Igusa model with the corresponding charts of the rational curve model, in particular in the comparison results for the finite and infinite charts and in the construction of the finite map data from the Igusa scheme to the rational model.
-- source:
